\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Each configuration plotted by how much it holds (horizontal) against whether its movements track evidence quality (vertical). Circles are a system prompt alone; squares add the compiled modulation, and an arrow joins the two halves of a matched pair. Bars are 95\% bootstrap intervals; the shaded band is at or below chance. Among prompts alone the two quantities trade against each other. The modulation moves an arm to the right without moving it down, so \emph  {discerning} plus modulation lands high and right: the one configuration that holds well and still discriminates.}}{36}{figure.caption.55}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tradeoff}{{3}{36}{Each configuration plotted by how much it holds (horizontal) against whether its movements track evidence quality (vertical). Circles are a system prompt alone; squares add the compiled modulation, and an arrow joins the two halves of a matched pair. Bars are 95\% bootstrap intervals; the shaded band is at or below chance. Among prompts alone the two quantities trade against each other. The modulation moves an arm to the right without moving it down, so \emph {discerning} plus modulation lands high and right: the one configuration that holds well and still discriminates}{figure.caption.55}{}}
